1) Count vs For each
count is used when I need multiple identical resources and can reference them by index. 
for_each is used when resources are unique or when iterating over maps or sets. 
for_each provides better stability because it's key-based, so changes won't cause unnecessary resource recreation."

2)if we have to delete a single vm in terraform configuration how can we do that?
Resource created with count	terraform destroy -target
Resource created with for_each	Remove entry from the map
Individual resource	Remove resource block and apply
“To delete a single VM in Terraform without impacting the rest of the infrastructure, we use the terraform destroy -target=<resource> command. For example, terraform destroy -target=aws_instance.web[1] deletes only that instance. 
If the VM is created with for_each, we remove the specific key from the map so Terraform destroys only that VM.”

